{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39659792",
      "title": "Rendering Multi-Dimensional Lists",
      "sourceHash": "25f3fdb228c7e651496445e7a5f5bc2b79fa03b90e59318c0ec86101c6d7b71a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 1.44,
          "en": "So now that we're able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.44,
          "end": 4.74,
          "en": "to edit those names here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.74,
          "end": 9.42,
          "en": "this player functionality is finished for the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.42,
          "end": 12.24,
          "en": "and we can therefore move on to the next building block,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.24,
          "end": 14.16,
          "en": "which is the game board.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.16,
          "end": 16.86,
          "en": "And here the goal is to output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.86,
          "end": 19.5,
          "en": "such a typical tic-tac-toe game board.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.5,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "So a three-by-three grid in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 24.21,
          "en": "And of course that should be a grid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.21,
          "end": 27.18,
          "en": "populated with buttons that can be clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.18,
          "end": 30.81,
          "en": "so that we can then also play the actual game.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.81,
          "end": 33.54,
          "en": "Therefore, here, I'll start by adding a new component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.54,
          "end": 38.523,
          "en": "the GameBoard component in a GameBoard.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.3,
          "end": 45.813,
          "en": "And in this component, I want to output such a grid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.65,
          "end": 49.71,
          "en": "So therefore here, I'll output an ordered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.71,
          "end": 51.51,
          "en": "Could also be an unordered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.51,
          "end": 52.83,
          "en": "Not too important here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.83,
          "end": 55.89,
          "en": "but I guess theoretically the order matters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.89,
          "end": 58.44,
          "en": "And I'll give that list an ID of game-board,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.44,
          "end": 60.78,
          "en": "again for styling reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.78,
          "end": 64.11,
          "en": "And then in there, we want to have three rows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.11,
          "end": 67.8,
          "en": "And then in those rows, we want to have three columns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.8,
          "end": 70.83,
          "en": "So a nested ordered list in every list item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.83,
          "end": 73.203,
          "en": "that's kind of the structure we want to have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.78999999999999,
          "end": 78.39,
          "en": "But I don't want to hard code this entire board,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 81.06,
          "en": "not just because that would be annoying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.06,
          "end": 83.28,
          "en": "but also because eventually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.28,
          "end": 86.49,
          "en": "this board needs to update dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.49,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "When we click on one of these squares in the board,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 93.72,
          "en": "we want to populate it with the symbol of the player",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.72,
          "end": 96.33,
          "en": "that clicked the square after all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.33,
          "end": 100.44,
          "en": "So ultimately, this should be a dynamically-derived board",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.44,
          "end": 103.47,
          "en": "and that's why I'll not hard code it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.47,
          "end": 107.49000000000001,
          "en": "Instead, for the moment here, we can simply add a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.49000000000001,
          "end": 109.74000000000001,
          "en": "outside of the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.74000000000001,
          "end": 112.47,
          "en": "because it's not some state or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 114.42,
          "en": "just a constant that allows me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.42,
          "end": 116.85,
          "en": "to outsource and store a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.85,
          "end": 119.17,
          "en": "And I'll name it initialGameBoard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.81,
          "end": 123.87,
          "en": "And this should be an array full of arrays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 125.4,
          "en": "because we need a grid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.4,
          "end": 128.37,
          "en": "So an array populated with three arrays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.37,
          "end": 132.27,
          "en": "where every array should hold three values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.27,
          "end": 135.48,
          "en": "And the idea here is, in the end, to have a game board",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.48,
          "end": 138.75,
          "en": "where some squares are empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.75,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "which could be represented by the value null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 146.1,
          "en": "and some squares might be populated with an X or an O,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.1,
          "end": 149.07,
          "en": "depending on which player clicked that square,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.07,
          "end": 152.28,
          "en": "so that we store the current state of the game",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.28,
          "end": 154.893,
          "en": "in a multi-dimensional array like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.85,
          "end": 159.78,
          "en": "Now initially, of course, all these squares are empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.78,
          "end": 163.203,
          "en": "so it's an array full of arrays, full of nulls.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.34,
          "end": 166.98,
          "en": "But we can now use this initial game board here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.98,
          "end": 168.48,
          "en": "to dynamically output it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.48,
          "end": 171.96,
          "en": "and dynamically render those grid items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.96,
          "end": 174.48,
          "en": "And we can again do this by using the map method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.48,
          "end": 176.433,
          "en": "as you learned before in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.42000000000002,
          "end": 179.22,
          "en": "Now the map method, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.22,
          "end": 181.29,
          "en": "takes a function as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.29,
          "end": 183.81,
          "en": "a function that will be called automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.81,
          "end": 185.67,
          "en": "for every item in that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.67,
          "end": 188.04,
          "en": "So in the end here for every nested array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.04,
          "end": 190.89,
          "en": "because these three nested arrays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.89,
          "end": 193.263,
          "en": "are the items in this outer array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.19,
          "end": 198.15,
          "en": "And therefore here, we'll get our row in the end, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.15,
          "end": 200.343,
          "en": "if these are our three rows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.14,
          "end": 205.07999999999998,
          "en": "And for every row, we want to output a list item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.07999999999998,
          "end": 209.52,
          "en": "And every list item, as you learned, needs a key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.52,
          "end": 213.32999999999998,
          "en": "a key so that it can be identified in a unique way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.32999999999998,
          "end": 216.45,
          "en": "Now here we don't really have a great unique key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.45,
          "end": 219.39,
          "en": "for these different arrays in the array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.39,
          "end": 222.21,
          "en": "and therefore here, I'll simply use the second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.21,
          "end": 226.05,
          "en": "that you can use here in this function you pass to map,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.05,
          "end": 229.62,
          "en": "which will simply be the current index of the item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.62,
          "end": 231.69299999999998,
          "en": "for which this function is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.56,
          "end": 236.37,
          "en": "And I'll use this index, which I here named rowIndex,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.37,
          "end": 237.933,
          "en": "as a value for the key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 238.82999999999998,
          "end": 242.55,
          "en": "In most cases, you want to avoid using this index here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.55,
          "end": 247.41,
          "en": "because this is not strictly tied to this value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.41,
          "end": 251.13,
          "en": "Because if this row here would swap place with the next row,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 251.13,
          "end": 254.4,
          "en": "technically this row would now have the index zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 254.4,
          "end": 257.79,
          "en": "even though this row had the index zero before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 257.79,
          "end": 261.33,
          "en": "So the index is not tied to the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.33,
          "end": 263.61,
          "en": "but to the position of the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.61,
          "end": 266.52,
          "en": "But here in this use case, that's no problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.52,
          "end": 269.88,
          "en": "Also because we're not going to swap any rows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 269.88,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "and therefore using the index here is fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 274.62,
          "en": "But now inside of that list item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.62,
          "end": 277.92,
          "en": "I want to have another list, another ordered list let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 277.92,
          "end": 281.4,
          "en": "where I want to output these values inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.4,
          "end": 284.85,
          "en": "of these inner arrays because we need a grid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 284.85,
          "end": 286.35,
          "en": "And at the moment, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 286.35,
          "end": 288.213,
          "en": "we just have a couple of rows here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 289.35,
          "end": 291.63,
          "en": "So in this ordered list here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 291.63,
          "end": 295.8,
          "en": "we again want to output something dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 295.8,
          "end": 297.84000000000003,
          "en": "and that something is that row,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 297.84000000000003,
          "end": 300.15,
          "en": "because that's this inner array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 300.15,
          "end": 302.94,
          "en": "three times this inner array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 302.94,
          "end": 306.48,
          "en": "So here we want to go through the items in this inner array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 306.48,
          "end": 309.21,
          "en": "again with map, to get our columns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 309.21,
          "end": 311.73,
          "en": "in the end and their index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 311.73,
          "end": 315.813,
          "en": "So to get these null values and their indexes in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 316.74,
          "end": 320.01,
          "en": "And then for every inner value in this inner array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 320.01,
          "end": 322.17,
          "en": "we again want to output a list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 322.17,
          "end": 324.843,
          "en": "where the key is set to colIndex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 327.51,
          "end": 328.68,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 328.68,
          "end": 331.86,
          "en": "And in that list item, we now finally then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 331.86,
          "end": 334.35,
          "en": "want to have a button that can be clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 334.35,
          "end": 337.95,
          "en": "And here I got a tiny error which must be fixed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 337.95,
          "end": 340.5,
          "en": "This closing parentheses belongs here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 340.5,
          "end": 343.59000000000003,
          "en": "But now here between these button tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 343.59000000000003,
          "end": 346.74,
          "en": "I want to output either an X if this button was clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 346.74,
          "end": 350.13,
          "en": "by the user who has the symbol X,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 350.13,
          "end": 354.3,
          "en": "or an O if it was the user with the symbol O,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.3,
          "end": 357.03,
          "en": "or nothing if the button was not clicked yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 357.03,
          "end": 359.25,
          "en": "And therefore this will be my initial state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.25,
          "end": 362.58,
          "en": "that I have no value between those button tags here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 362.58,
          "end": 363.78,
          "en": "To be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 363.78,
          "end": 368.01,
          "en": "the dynamic value I want to output here is my col.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 368.01,
          "end": 371.22,
          "en": "So this value here, which initially is null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 371.22,
          "end": 372.36,
          "en": "and if we output null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 372.36,
          "end": 375.18,
          "en": "nothing will be visible on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 375.18,
          "end": 377.88,
          "en": "And here I need an extra pair of parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 377.88,
          "end": 380.523,
          "en": "around these two parameters for this to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 381.42,
          "end": 385.41,
          "en": "And since col for column here is not an ideal name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 385.41,
          "end": 389.463,
          "en": "I'll rename this col parameter to playerSymbol,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 391.86,
          "end": 394.08,
          "en": "also here so that it's clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 394.08,
          "end": 395.73,
          "en": "that it will be the playerSymbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 395.73,
          "end": 397.98,
          "en": "that will be shown between these button tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 399.42,
          "end": 400.253,
          "en": "But with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 400.253,
          "end": 404.13,
          "en": "I'm now outputting this grid here dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 404.13,
          "end": 407.1,
          "en": "Of course, at the moment, there's no way of changing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 407.1,
          "end": 410.64,
          "en": "We don't really do anything if these buttons get clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 410.64,
